#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "c. Compute backward bounds {#c-compute-backward-bounds}"
msgstr "c. Menghitung backward bounds {#c-compute-backward-bounds}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This part of noise prediction evaluates how an error at a particular layer can affect the input state $\\rho$. The `compute_backward_bounds` function first inverts the circuit and removes measurement gates, and then proceeds with a similar analysis as was done for the forward-bound computations.\n"
msgstr "Bagian dari prediksi noise ini mengevaluasi bagaimana error pada layer tertentu dapat memengaruhi input state $\\rho$. Fungsi `compute_backward_bounds` pertama-tama membalik circuit dan menghapus gate measurement, lalu melanjutkan dengan analisis yang serupa dengan yang dilakukan untuk perhitungan forward-bound.\n"

#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Visualize the SLC for manual inspection {#visualize-the-slc-for-manual-inspection-2}"
msgstr "Memvisualisasikan SLC untuk inspeksi manual {#visualize-the-slc-for-manual-inspection-2}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "From computing backward bounds, we can see how the initial state structure governs the early behavior of error propagation:\n"
msgstr "Dari perhitungan backward bounds, kita bisa melihat bagaimana struktur initial state mengatur perilaku awal dari propagasi error:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can clearly see how the Z errors initially commute with the |0⟩ initial state.\n"
msgstr "Kita bisa dengan jelas melihat bagaimana error Z awalnya berkomutasi dengan initial state |0⟩.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Only on qubit 6, where we initialize the +1 eigenstate of the X basis, does a Z error fail to commute, while an X error does commute.\n"
msgstr "Hanya pada qubit 6, di mana kita menginisialisasi eigenstate +1 dari basis X, error Z gagal berkomutasi, sementara error X berkomutasi.\n"

